  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "The operator workstation is untrusted: only a signed session crosses inward, and the scraper carries a JWT",
        "The backoffice host runs outside the cluster - the cluster accepts the gateway only as a queue publisher",
        "Gemini is the only LLM call, and Telegram the only other outbound request"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Queue contract",
      "items": [
        "resumes.generate and resumes.cover each own a DLX/DLQ and a ScaledObject; prefetch_count = 1",
        "The topology is declared three times - chart Secret, utils/messaging.py, backoffice queue.ts - and a mismatch makes RabbitMQ answer 406",
        "Retries climb RETRY_LADDER_SECONDS, and the message is acked only after persist returns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Graph control flow",
      "items": [
        "adapt_text short-circuits to persist when nothing matched in the DOCX",
        "vision_check loops back to adapt_text until approved or MAX_REVISIONS is spent",
        "persist is the mandatory terminal node, and the ack follows it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Artifacts and the master CV",
      "items": [
        "/data holds cv_data.json and input/cv.docx, which must stay verbatim in sync - one whitespace mismatch fails the task",
        "The stored paths are served through GET /api/artifacts/<job_id>?format=docx",
        "The cv-files helper pod keeps the volume reachable while the worker sits at zero replicas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scheduled automation",
      "items": [
        "Scout runs 0,30 7-23 * * * and writes Scraped cards plus one Telegram message - never a queue message, never Gemini",
        "The archiver refuses Applied cards left untouched for 10 days and deletes nothing",
        "Both append one process_runs row per run; a dry run writes nothing"
      ]
    }
  ]
